<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Canning Hill</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bukit Larangan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Canning Hill is a hill in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a> overlooking the Singapore River. Malay tradition remembers it as Bukit Larangan, the Forbidden Hill of the kings of Singapura, and excavations there have found 14th-century Chinese ceramics, gold ornaments and workshop remains. The British built Government House on it after 1819 and later Fort Canning, from which it takes its name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-canning-hill.jpg" alt="Fort Canning Hill" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LN9267 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fort_Canning_Park_09-11-2023(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
